{
 "comment": "tds_payees, #1243: the client's list of reversals names a voucher by its GUID, so it reads on every voucher holding it. Builder N: two reversals sharing one GUID, classified as credit notes: both are named. Builder R: two blank-GUID reversals, the blank GUID classified as a credit note: both are named. Builder P: a bill-specific reversal names a GUID two of its bills share: classified, against either. Builder M: eleven bills share one GUID and a reversal names it as a duplicate or error: against each, in the books' order. Builders Q1 and Q2: one GUID on a bill to each; a bill-specific reversal on Q2 names it, against Q2's bill only. A listed reversal GUID no voucher holds is reported as matching nothing.",
